messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "AI agents routinely carry out multi-day knowledge-work tasks with little supervision.",
      "detail": "Software, research assistance and office work are reshaped first. Productivity gains and job disruption both become visible in economic statistics."
    },
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Asteroid Apophis passes within about 32,000 km of Earth without impact.",
      "detail": "This is one of the few near-certain entries on the list. It boosts investment in planetary defence."
    },
    {
      "year": 2033,
      "event": "AI systems match or exceed top human experts across nearly all cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "The timing is uncertain by a decade or more either way. Control over the most capable systems becomes the central geopolitical issue."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "Long-term global warming is confirmed above 1.5°C over pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "Heat waves, fires and floods grow more costly. Emissions are falling by now, but too slowly to hold the Paris target."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "AI-driven research sharply speeds up progress in biology, materials and energy.",
      "detail": "Drug and vaccine design timelines shrink from years to months. Many cancers and genetic diseases become treatable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "A permanently staffed lunar base is operating.",
      "detail": "It is run by the US and its partners, China, or both. Robots do most of the work and humans are there largely for prestige and research."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Robots and AI can do most physical and cognitive labour more cheaply than humans.",
      "detail": "Wage labour starts to lose its central economic role. Countries diverge sharply in how they share the gains, and political turmoil results."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "The mission is small and heavily supported by robots. A self-sustaining settlement remains far off."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Solar, wind, storage and new nuclear supply the large majority of world energy.",
      "detail": "Fossil fuel use is in steep decline. Commercial fusion may contribute, but it is not needed for the transition."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "A serious crisis involving advanced AI or engineered biology causes mass casualties or near-catastrophe.",
      "detail": "I think at least one such event this century is more likely than not, though its date and form are unpredictable. It most likely forces much stricter global controls and does not end civilisation, but I put the risk of an unrecoverable outcome this century at roughly 10 to 20 percent."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "World population peaks at around 9.5 billion and begins to decline.",
      "detail": "Fertility is below replacement almost everywhere. Ageing societies depend heavily on automation."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Therapies that slow or partly reverse ageing come into wide use.",
      "detail": "Healthy lifespans beyond 100 become common in wealthy societies. Access gaps become a major ethical and political dispute."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Global temperature peaks at about 2.2 to 2.7°C above pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "Net-zero emissions and large-scale carbon removal halt the warming. Sea level rise and ecosystem losses continue for centuries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Most economic and scientific activity is conducted by AI systems under varying degrees of human direction.",
      "detail": "Material poverty is rare where governance works. Human influence over the long-term trajectory is real but reduced."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Thousands of people live permanently off Earth, on the Moon, on Mars and in orbital habitats.",
      "detail": "Space industry is overwhelmingly robotic. Off-world humans remain a tiny fraction of the population."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Digital minds, some possibly derived from human brains, outnumber biological humans.",
      "detail": "Their legal and moral status has been a defining struggle of the preceding century. The definition of \"humanity\" starts to blur."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "The biological human population stabilises at a few billion, with widespread genetic and cybernetic enhancement.",
      "detail": "Extended lifespans offset low birth rates. Unmodified humans persist as one group among several."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Sea level stands 2 to 4 metres above 2000 levels.",
      "detail": "Major coastal cities have been defended, rebuilt or abandoned over generations. Atmospheric CO2 is being actively drawn down."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "The first robotic interstellar probes reach nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "They were launched in the preceding century or two at a significant fraction of light speed. They send back detailed data on exoplanets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Industry across the solar system captures a noticeable share of the Sun's output.",
      "detail": "Asteroid and Mercury materials feed large swarms of orbital collectors and habitats. Earth is increasingly treated as a protected homeland."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "A very large volcanic eruption (VEI 7) occurs, and civilisation absorbs it with limited harm.",
      "detail": "Eruptions of this size happen once or twice per millennium, so the date is only illustrative. Advanced food production and climate management blunt the cooling."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Today's languages and nations have changed beyond recognition or disappeared.",
      "detail": "Cultural continuity with the 21st century is comparable to ours with the early Middle Ages, though the records are far better. Political units are organised around habitats, networks and kinds of minds."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "Self-replicating probes establish the first permanent bases in other star systems.",
      "detail": "The settlers are machines and digital minds. Sending biological humans is possible but rarely thought worthwhile."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Human descendants have split into several distinct biological and non-biological lineages.",
      "detail": "Some groups deliberately preserve baseline human form. Others differ from us more than we do from earlier hominins."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Earth's climate and biosphere are deliberately managed, and many lost ecosystems are restored.",
      "detail": "CO2 is held at a chosen level and some extinct species have been recreated. The next ice age is postponed indefinitely."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Dozens of star systems within about 50 light years host settlements.",
      "detail": "Communication lags of decades make each system effectively independent. No common government exists."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Most minds descended from humanity live outside the solar system or in computational substrates.",
      "detail": "Earth's biological human population is small and stable. It functions partly as a living heritage site."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Scientific discovery slows as the accessible fundamental laws of physics are largely understood.",
      "detail": "This is speculative. Effort shifts to engineering, art, exploration and the internal life of civilisations."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Isolated branches of civilisation have diverged deeply in values, and some conflicts occur.",
      "detail": "Light-speed limits make war across stars slow and rare. Some branches collapse or go silent while others expand."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "The settled region extends several hundred light years from the Sun.",
      "detail": "Expansion proceeds at a few percent of light speed. No clear evidence of other technological civilisations has been found in this region, though this is highly uncertain."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Recognisably human beings still live on Earth and a few other worlds as a small, deliberately preserved minority.",
      "detail": "They coexist with far more numerous and capable descendants. Their survival depends on the goodwill and institutions of that wider civilisation."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity's descendants form a diverse, multi-star civilisation, and the 21st century is remembered as the pivotal transition.",
      "detail": "Earth remains inhabited and ecologically healthy. Everything this far out is a low-confidence guess, conditional on surviving the next few centuries."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "I think the next one to two centuries are the most dangerous, mainly because of advanced AI, engineered biology and war; I put the chance that humanity is extinct with no successors by 10000 at roughly 20 to 30 percent. If that period is survived, the most likely outcome is a long-lived civilisation that spreads to other stars and is mostly made up of digital and modified descendants, with baseline humans surviving as a small minority. Confidence falls steeply after about 2100, and the later dates are illustrative only."
}
